        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Supplemental Material for \"Passive Seismic Study of a magma-dominated rift: the Salton Trough\" ,Shahar Barak's PhD dissertation.\r\n\r\nSupplemental files for Chapter 2: \"San Andreas Fault dip, Peninsular Ranges mafic lower crust and partial melt in the Salton Trough, Southern California, from ambient-noise tomography\" start with the ggge20875 prefix.\r\n\r\nSupplemental files for Chapter 3: \"Rapid variation in upper-mantle rheology across the San Andreas fault system and Salton Trough, southernmost California, USA\" start with the 2016190 prefix.\r\n\r\nThe file StationsMetadata.zip contains Word documents detailing station locations, photos, driving directions and other metadata, and two Excel files containing information used for the stations' deployment, servicing and demobilization.",
